:{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104333","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104333.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104333.patch","merged_at":"2025-04-08T17:46:51Z"},"body":"Continuation of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99002 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/95774\r\n\r\nThis PR addressed yet **yet** another huge chunk of class reference oddities I remembered to note down for later while localizing the class reference. Some of these are clear typos, some are inconsistencies, some are just awkward.\r\n\r\nOh boy this will be nasty for localization.\r\n\r\nOf particular note:\r\n- Replaced the single use of \"govern\" with a more common verb\r\n- Elaborated slightly more on **DisplayServer**'s `screen_get_image` and `screen_get_image_rect`\r\n- ~~Tweaked EditorExportPlatformAndroid's `screen/immersive_mode` to actually mention immersive mode~~\r\n- Went ballistic on Skeleton3D's `metadata`-related descriptions\r\n- Filled many glTF definitions with appropriate `[code]` tags.\r\n- Fixed a common \"will be return\" typo in the **SCALING_MODE** constants\r\n- Fixed some missing articles (especially where it looked inconsistent with the rest)\r\n- Fixed `vertex_buffer_create` glaringly missing what it actually created.\r\n- Fixed **OS**'s `read_buffer_from_stdin` mentioning the wrong method\r\n- Fixed **GLTFAccessor**'s `accessor_type` mentioning corresponding **int** values even though it's an enum\r\n\t- The description was copied from the deprecated `type` property without accounting for this\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/fol